== Cleaning Products: Gather and Check

Bring every cleaner, spray and refill to one table. You will find duplicates and bottles you forgot. Many products carry a date or a "best by" mark on the label. If there is no date, use what you know: a product that has separated, changed color or smells off is ready to go.

#v(0.1in)
#_wk-table(
  (1fr, 3.6em, 3.6em, 3.6em, 3.6em),
  ([Product or type], [Keep], [Donate], [Sell], [Toss]),
  (
    [All-purpose and glass cleaners],
    [Bathroom and toilet cleaners],
    [Kitchen and oven cleaners],
    [Dish and laundry soap],
    [Sponges, brushes and cloths],
    [Air fresheners and polishes],
    [Half-empty bottles of the same product],
    [Products I never use],
  ),
  extra: 2, y: 9.5pt,
)

#v(0.15in)
#checklist(none, (
  [I checked every label for a date and tossed expired or unsafe-looking products],
  [Each product is in its original container with the label readable],
  [I did not mix products, and I will not mix them while pouring leftovers together],
  [For anything hazardous, I will check my local household hazardous waste guidelines before it leaves the house],
))

